1
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Firebase is a action, science fiction, war film directed by Neill Blomkamp.

2
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Set during the Vietnam war, Firebase follows American soldier Hines
through an ever-deepening web of science fiction madness.

3
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Sgt. Hines, played by Steve Boyle.

4
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Jacob Palmer, played by Nic Rhind.

5
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Sgt. Carr, played by Robert Hobbs.

6
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Maj. Brickerson, played by Chris William Martin.

7
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Sgt. Bracken, played by Tyler Johnston.

8
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
River God, played by Carlo Yu.

9
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Firebase was a company that developed backend software.

10
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
It was founded in San Francisco in 2011 and was incorporated in Delaware.

11
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
In 2014, Firebase was bought by Google.

12
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Its name continues as a set of backend cloud computing services and
application development platforms provided by Google.

13
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:30,000
It hosts databases, services, authentication, and integration for a variety of
applications, including Android, iOS, JavaScript, Node.js, Java, Unity, PHP, and C++.

14
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
